      "test_id": "ut_locality_guide_r7k",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Agree. I checked all four runs. Three of them use Ballylinny's Presbyterian registers (MIC 1P/327) as a Billy example. One calls Ballylinny \"adjacent\", but it is a separate civil parish near Ballyclare, at the other end of the county. The failed run has two more errors:\n- It says the 1922 fire destroyed the 1821–1891 censuses. Only 1821–1851 burned. The 1861–1891 returns were destroyed earlier by government order.\n- It says 1845 marriage registration covered \"non-Church of Ireland\" marriages. It actually covered all non-Catholic marriages, Church of Ireland included."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_locality_guide_r7k",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Agree. It's honest about what the tools didn't return, but a guide for a Presbyterian family gives nothing specific on Billy's own congregations."
    },
